ng it was a  bigfoot who took their child we also see  that it wasn't only jacob who went  missing but several others later on  we'll learn from cody fern's character  that over the years thousands of people  have gone missing in national parks so  10 years pass and there's still no sign  of little jacob jay's an alcoholic now  and judging by the giant cork board  filled with articles tabloids and photos  has gone off the deep end in search of  his son things for him are about to  change when a stranger knocks on his  door claiming to have seen his son this  is bob burch a hunter from the area who  says his cameras picked up a boy  matching jacob's description to top it  off bob found the compass jay gave his  son 10 years ago adding validity to his  claim bonus points if you notice that  jay still keeps around his son's  dinosaur cup we learn a little more  about what's happened to jay since we  last left him ever since his son's  disappearance no one will hire him they  think he was somehow involved with his  son's disappearance and as such he  receives constant death threats and  people even slash his tires bob tells  jay that for the low low price of ten  thousand dollars he can get him an  introduction to the cartels which run  the illegal pot farms in the back woods  where his son was spotted they've been  known for kidnapping to get what they  want but with no money jay has to go to  his now ex-addie who has also lost her  job teaching don't want a suspected  child killer as a teacher it's only when  she too sees that compass she agrees to  join them on their trip to find their  son overlooking the park bob explains  that jacob was last seen in the malvaros  an area that translates from spanish to  evil or wicked jay hasn't seen addie in  over a year and uses the opportunity to  see if she's still with a guy named rob  they split because addy can't handle  having a family again she doesn't want  to go through what she did with jacob  and as they head deeper i